 {"id": "DOC-10", "title": "P4 — README Status + docs/RELEASE.md still present v0.1.0 as the only tag and 0.1.2 as the unreleased stamp after the v0.2.0 cut", "status": "pending", "priority": "P4", "created_by": null, "reasoning": "DOC ROT, measured 2026-11-16 at origin/main 7788fb4. Doc severity is P4 by Bane ruling 2026-09-30 (documentation findings never outrank functional defects); P4 is this row being filed, NOT a new assessment of severity.\n\nCLAIM IN DOCS\n- README.md:373-376 — \"Development version stamp **0.1.2** — **not released**: built from source, no tag. Tag **v0.1.0** (2026-09-24) is the last shipped version; it is the repo only tag and its only GitHub Release object (commit c655666) — the tree is **over 160 commits** past it.\"\n- docs/RELEASE.md:8 — \"Existing tags: v0.1.0.\"\n\nREALITY (commands run, outputs pasted)\n$ git for-each-ref --format=%(refname:short) %(creatordate:short) %(subject) refs/tags\nv0.1.0 2026-09-24 v0.1.0 — first tagged release: match/compile/validate/consult/gate/absorb CLI, 10-class closed registry...\nv0.2.0 2026-11-16 lore v0.2.0\n$ git ls-remote --tags origin\n... refs/tags/v0.2.0 9f605bae671ae0f688847b204db8e4fc3dce22ce\n... refs/tags/v0.2.0^{} 165cc8f6d354d9ed57d58635c1ad482d0e755cf2\n$ git merge-base --is-ancestor v0.2.0 origin/main -> exit 0 (v0.2.0 is on the published tip)\n$ grep -n version pyproject.toml -> 7:version = \"0.2.0\"\n$ grep -n __version__ lore/__init__.py -> 3:__version__ = \"0.2.0\"\n$ head -12 CHANGELOG.md -> 9:## [0.2.0] — 2026-11-16 (promoted section, not marked Not released)\n$ git rev-list --count v0.1.0..HEAD -> 415   (README says \"over 160\")\n$ sed -n 1,40p docs/release-evidence/lore-releng-2026-11-16-23-09-49.txt -> \"hosted CI (tag) release-check completed/success run 23:36:14Z\"; \"gh run list release-check success on push/v0.2.0 @165cc8f\"\n\nIMPACT: the first status paragraph a reader sees declares the project unreleased with one tag, while the current tree is v0.2.0, tagged on origin 